---
// 3.3: who is who in a company: shareholders own it, directors run it, officers manage it day to day.
---
<figure class="cs-fig su-fig" data-cr>
  <span class="cs-figtag">Diagram: who owns, who decides, who runs it</span>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 600 230" role="img" aria-label="Shareholders elect directors; directors appoint officers; the company is a separate person that owns assets and signs contracts">
    <g data-r="sh" style="cursor:pointer"><rect x="20" y="15" width="170" height="54" rx="10" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="105" y="47" text-anchor="middle" style="font-weight:700">Shareholders</text></g>
    <g data-r="dir" style="cursor:pointer"><rect x="20" y="88" width="170" height="54" rx="10" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="105" y="120" text-anchor="middle" style="font-weight:700">Directors (board)</text></g>
    <g data-r="off" style="cursor:pointer"><rect x="20" y="161" width="170" height="54" rx="10" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="105" y="193" text-anchor="middle" style="font-weight:700">Officers (CEO, CFO)</text></g>
    <path d="M105 69 V88 M105 142 V161" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#cr-a)"/>
    <defs><marker id="cr-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="var(--accent)"/></marker></defs>
    <text x="114" y="83" class="mu" style="font-size:11px">elect</text><text x="114" y="156" style="font-size:11px">appoint</text>
    <g data-r="co" style="cursor:pointer"><rect x="300" y="60" width="280" height="110" rx="14" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2.5"/><text x="440" y="100" text-anchor="middle" style="font-weight:700">The company</text><text x="440" y="122" text-anchor="middle">a separate legal person:</text><text x="440" y="142" text-anchor="middle">owns, signs, sues, owes, pays tax</text></g>
    <path d="M190 115 H296" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4"/>
  </svg>
  <div class="su-card on"><strong data-t>Tap a box</strong><div data-d>One person can wear all three hats: a solo founder is often the only shareholder, the only director and the CEO.</div></div>
  <figcaption>The names differ a little: India's Companies Act says "members" for shareholders and requires at least one resident director; US corporations name officers such as a president and secretary; Canadian law says "directors" and "officers" much like the US.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
  const R: Record<string, [string, string]> = {
    sh: ['Shareholders (members)', 'Own the company through shares. They vote to elect directors and on big changes (selling the company, changing the articles). They are not liable for its debts beyond what they paid for their shares.'],
    dir: ['Directors', 'Make the big decisions as a board and owe the company duties of care and loyalty. Directors can be personally liable for some things, such as unpaid employee wages or tax deducted at source that was never paid over.'],
    off: ['Officers', 'Run the business day to day under the board: the CEO, CFO, secretary. In a small startup the founders are usually all of these at once.'],
    co: ['The company', 'Exists separately from the people in it. It keeps going if a founder leaves, can raise money by selling new shares, and files its own tax return.'],
  };
  for (const fig of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cr]')) fig.querySelectorAll<SVGGElement>('[data-r]').forEach((g) => g.addEventListener('click', () => { const [t, d] = R[g.dataset.r!]; fig.querySelector('[data-t]')!.textContent = t; fig.querySelector('[data-d]')!.textContent = d; fig.querySelectorAll<SVGGElement>('[data-r] rect').forEach((r) => r.setAttribute('stroke-width', r.parentElement === g ? '4' : '2')); }));
</script>
